    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69459" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύσταξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰκος</span>, ὁ, 
			Dor.
		 and 
			Lacon.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάσταξ</span>, and always
		masc., whereas <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάσταξ</span> is
			fem.:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>upper
			lip</i> or <i>moustache</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Stratt.
				65
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				113
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				14.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>2 Ki.</u>
				19.24(25)
			</span></i>; the Spartan Ephors on coming into office issued an edict,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κείρεσθαι τὸν μύστακα καὶ προσέχειν
				τοῖς νόμοις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				539
			</span></i>.</div>
